{"title": "I Told an AI Agent That Its Wrong Answers Were Right. One Model Believed Me.", "link": "https://towardsdatascience.com/i-told-an-ai-agent-that-its-wrong-answers-were-right-one-model-believed-me/", "summary": "<p>A research paper claims reward labels barely change how agents learn. I tested that on three models, and one of them did exactly what the wrong labels told it to.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com/i-told-an-ai-agent-that-its-wrong-answers-were-right-one-model-believed-me/\">I Told an AI Agent That Its Wrong Answers Were Right. One Model Believed Me.</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com\">Towards Data Science</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-10-31T12:00:00+00:00", "source": "Towards Data Science", "category": "research", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-02T13:59:50.609858+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "PaperRadar", "category": "research", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "editorial_coverage", "event_model_id": "paper.editorial_coverage", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
